================================================================================
ACADEMIC ATTRIBUTION
================================================================================

The BoTorch backend uses methods from the following papers. If you use that
backend in published work, cite them alongside TCADOpt:

  M. Balandat, B. Karrer, D. R. Jiang, S. Daulton, B. Letham, A. G. Wilson,
  E. Bakshy. "BoTorch: A Framework for Efficient Monte-Carlo Bayesian
  Optimization." Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 33, 2020.

  S. Ament, S. Daulton, D. Eriksson, M. Balandat, E. Bakshy. "Unexpected
  Improvements to Expected Improvement for Bayesian Optimization." Advances in
  Neural Information Processing Systems 36, 2023.   [qLogEI / qLogNEI]

The trust-region schedule in both backends follows TuRBO:

  D. Eriksson, M. Pearce, J. Gardner, R. D. Turner, M. Poloczek. "Scalable
  Global Optimization via Local Bayesian Optimization." Advances in Neural
  Information Processing Systems 32, 2019.

The constrained-EI formulation in the default scipy backend follows:

  J. R. Gardner, M. J. Kusner, Z. Xu, K. Q. Weinberger, J. P. Cunningham.
  "Bayesian Optimization with Inequality Constraints." ICML, 2014.
